WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.170
Hold up!

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:04.850
Before we go any further, make sure you’ve
watched our previous three videos on the epic

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.400
saga of Pietro Wilson and SCP - 5000 - The
Suit.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.780
What we’re talking about here probably won’t
make much sense if you don’t.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.170
Go ahead, we’ll wait…

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:16.170
Okay?

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.170
Good.

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:21.760
Last time we left Pietro Wilson, he was dead...and
also, somehow, alive.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.349
It seemed that, in the last moments of his
life, Wilson left a kind of nightmare dimension

00:00:26.349 --> 00:00:31.250
where the SCP Foundation had become evil,
and was transported back to our world as a

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.780
corpse in the broken SCP - 5000.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.070
But is that really the case?

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:42.930
The fact is, the tale of Pietro Wilson and
SCP - 5000 is one of the most complex and

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.710
mysterious events in the SCP universe.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:50.219
You’ve got questions, and we’ve got answers
- Why Pietro?

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:51.629
What was in the briefcase?

00:00:51.629 --> 00:00:54.180
What exactly happened at the end of the story?

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:59.790
And perhaps most importantly of all, why did
the SCP Foundation abandon their mission,

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:03.500
and make destroying all of humanity their
new primary directive?

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.830
Whenever you’re dealing with splintered
realities and mind-melting nightmares, there’s

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.480
bound to be a number of interpretations.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.860
And we’re eager to explain one of the more
popular ones right here.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:19.090
Soon, you’ll know it all - but to find out,
we need to start at the beginning.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:24.980
Our hero, Foundation employee Pietro Wilson,
was going about his day at Exclusionary Site-06.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:29.710
However, normal operations were interrupted
when a Mobile Task Force turned Foundation

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:35.090
Hit Squad stormed in and began executing employees
left and right as part of their wider plan

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.720
to wipe out humanity.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:42.500
Pietro got lucky though, and managed to find
SCP - 5000, making him undetectable to the

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.500
invading MTF squad.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.570
This brings us to our first questions: Why
Pietro?

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:52.030
And how does killing Foundation staff help
advance the O5 council’s goal of overthrowing

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.030
humanity?

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:57.140
The answer to both questions has everything
to do with the site that Pietro and his coworkers

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:01.790
were at when the attack went down - Exclusionary
Site-06.

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:06.030
Exclusionary Sites are a very special kind
of Foundation site that utilizes the same

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:11.080
technology as the Scranton Box - a container
used to protect important items from reality

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:14.750
warpers - but on a far more ambitious scale.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:18.890
Because of the use of this technology, these
Exclusionary Sites are essentially resistant

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:24.840
to CK-Class Restructuring Scenarios and Temporal
Anomalies, those are where reality and or

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.340
history itself are changed by a powerful entity.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:33.030
This makes them a perfect location for, say,
staff wanting to stage a revolt when their

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.790
leaders have decided to wipe out humanity.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:40.900
The Foundation wished to eliminate the personnel
stationed at these protected sites as a precautionary

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.810
measure, before moving onto the main phase
of their plan.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:49.590
But this attack was just one part of the Foundation’s
wider scheme to purge their ranks of dissenters

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.400
before putting their final mission into place.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.310
In order to make sure there were no internal
threats left who could pose a threat to the

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:01.460
new main directive, the Foundation murdered
all the staff at Exclusionary Sites, hunted

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:06.650
down and assassinated any resigned employees,
and killed off any humanoid or human-sympathetic

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.960
SCPs, leaving no one who could stop them.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.050
Or at least they thought there was no one
left…

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:17.930
While all of this was happening, Pietro suited
up and exited the site.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.040
So, why Pietro?

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:24.780
Because he got lucky, and he happened to stumble
upon SCP - 5000.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:29.380
He wasn’t the Chosen One, nor was he in
any way exceptional, beyond his willingness

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:32.880
to see his quest for answers through to the
bitter end.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:37.030
Pietro really could have been any of us if
we were in his situation.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:40.280
When Pietro escaped, he found the world in
disarray.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:46.700
SCPs had been released on a global scale - destroying
infrastructure, massacring civilians, and

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.650
assassinating key political figures.

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:55.020
The Foundation had even gone public, for the
first time ever, with their new intentions:

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.060
Destroy all humans.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:01.470
Pietro decided to head to Site-19 and get
to the bottom of their madness.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:05.959
On his way there, he saw a group of Mobile
Task Force members, performing a bizarre stabbing

00:04:05.959 --> 00:04:09.290
ritual to see who among them could feel pain.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.910
Remember this, it’ll be important later.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:17.320
Like a lot of small moments in the story of
SCP - 5000, these are puzzle pieces that can

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:21.470
be fit together to create the true picture
of what’s happening out of the chaos.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:26.510
At Site-19, among the dead-eyed Foundation
workers plotting mass killings, Pietro found

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:29.080
a treasure trove of vital information.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:33.380
There he learned about the existence of Project
PNEUMA, an O5 Council-approved initiative

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:38.550
to map out the human psychosphere - otherwise
known as the collective unconscious.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:43.480
He also found a redacted unanimous vote from
the O5 Council and Ethics Committee, as well

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:47.870
as a redacted series of directives sent out
to Senior Staff and Site Directors, which

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:51.620
caused a wave of suicides and resignations.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:55.510
During his search, Pietro also discovered
a second series of directives sent out to

00:04:55.510 --> 00:05:01.370
the remaining Site Directors and Senior Staff,
including the phrase “Harden your heart.”

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:04.350
These directives are known to some as “The
Cure.”

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:08.740
While Pietro didn’t have the context to
put all this together yet, these are more

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.940
vital clues to what happened.

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:16.010
The PNEUMA Project is what incited the Foundation’s
motivation to destroy humanity - killing off

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:20.220
humans is actually secondary to eliminating
something hiding else that’s hiding within

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:25.949
the human psychosphere - again that’s the
collective unconsciousness of all humans.

00:05:25.949 --> 00:05:30.770
The O5 Council and the Ethics Committee were
unanimous in their approval of this project,

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:36.290
which was like deciding to burn down a house
to kill the inhabitant inside, except in this

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:39.070
scenario, humanity is the house.

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:41.530
So who or what exactly is the inhabitant?

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:43.830
You’ll find that out soon.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:47.910
The next thing Pietro knew, he was sitting
half way across the country, with no memory

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.960
of the previous three months.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:55.140
He was also carrying a briefcase with no knowledge
of what was inside except that it was“not

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:56.140
round.”

00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:02.280
He also had a strange compulsion to deliver
the briefcase to SCP - 579, for reasons he

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:07.940
didn’t fully understand, but he hoped that
doing so would lead him to some answers.

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:11.890
Pietro may not have known what he was holding,
but we do.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:18.360
The clue here is “not round” - which is
the only confirmed fact about SCP - 055, otherwise

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.300
known as The Anti-Meme.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:26.110
This is an SCP with the primary anomalous
property of literally being unknowable.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:30.990
People who observe it forget what they observed,
and have no memory of even looking at 055

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.470
in the first place.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:36.400
This is why the briefcase was able to act
as Pietro’s personal “Skip” button.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:40.510
Pietro was physically covering the distance
he traveled, but every time he opened the

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:46.949
briefcase and looked at SCP-055, he forgot
that period of time, making it seem as though

00:06:46.949 --> 00:06:49.530
he simply skipped forwards.

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:56.080
The thing he was skipping towards, SCP - 579,
is an equally mysterious and highly dangerous

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.669
SCP contained within Site-62C.

00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:05.400
Nobody even really knows what 579 is, only
that it’s an anomaly so dangerous that the

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:09.340
entirety of Site-62C was built to contain
it.

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:11.790
So what’s so important about bringing these
two together?

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:17.750
That, and the vital importance of Pietro’s
final mission, will become clear very soon.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:22.630
Pietro continued his journey with the briefcase,
encountering more horrors and countless deaths

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:23.979
upon the way.

00:07:23.979 --> 00:07:29.300
He finally found some solace in coming across
a group of Global Occult Coalition soldiers

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:34.540
discussing the interrogation of a captured
member of Foundation staff named Samuel Ross.

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:38.930
Two quotes from Ross’ enigmatic speech are
of particular interest here.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:44.080
The first, in response to the threat of torture,
was “Do what you want.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:50.110
Once you realize you're not supposed to feel
pain, there's nothing to be afraid of anymore.”

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:54.650
The second, after witnessing the death of
his captors, was “Look what you've done

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:55.650
to yourselves.

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:58.889
I told you you wouldn't like it, didn't you?

00:07:58.889 --> 00:08:01.270
That's why you hear your voice.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:03.350
But you wanted to know so badly.

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:08.979
I really liked you guys, so I was trying to
be nice.

00:08:08.979 --> 00:08:12.710
We're so kind to you, you know.

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:19.000
We fight in the light so you can die in the
dark...disgusting.”

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:23.220
Do these quotes sound a little familiar?

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:28.750
The first because, as Pietro himself recalled,
the MTF members getting stabbed earlier also

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:30.810
didn’t seem to feel pain.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:36.219
The second, because describing people as “disgusting”
is an adjective favoured by another infamous

00:08:36.219 --> 00:08:38.089
SCP...

00:08:38.089 --> 00:08:39.949
SCP-682.

00:08:39.949 --> 00:08:45.279
This brings us back to “The Cure” - the
document disseminated by the O5 Council, instructing

00:08:45.279 --> 00:08:47.470
people to “Harden Their Hearts.”

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:51.319
Whatever the Foundation discovered in the
human psychosphere, it’s apparently the

00:08:51.319 --> 00:08:57.240
cause of all pain, and hence, when the Foundation
discovered it, they were able to train themselves

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:58.240
out of pain.

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:04.610
And as for the SCP - 682 reference - This
is a being that despises life, and it’s

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:09.769
believed by some that the reason 682 holds
this belief is that it’s always known about

00:09:09.769 --> 00:09:13.529
whatever the Foundation recently discovered
through Project PNEUMA.

00:09:13.529 --> 00:09:18.100
Decrypted text logs in the Foundation files
confirm this in a documented exchange between

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:23.040
O5-1 and Tejani, the head of the Foundation
Ethics Committee.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:27.829
In their conversation they confirm the existence
of The Cure - which deprived the personnel

00:09:27.829 --> 00:09:33.910
of everything from pain to empathy - being
disseminated among staff prior to the massacre,

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:37.810
and of the Foundation’s sudden ideological
alignment with SCP - 682.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:46.079
And they had found something else too, referred
to simply as IT . Whatever IT was, it was

00:09:46.079 --> 00:09:49.779
the reason Foundation Command decided to wipe
out humanity.

00:09:49.779 --> 00:09:52.490
But what is IT?

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:56.660
What could possibly be so bad it was worth
killing all of humanity?

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:01.369
Perhaps most surprising of all is that Pietro
ran into the creature’s physical manifestation,

00:10:01.369 --> 00:10:05.660
and he barely even considered it - due to
being occupied by avoiding the attacks of

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:08.579
the statue like, mantis-armed “Blinkers.”

00:10:08.579 --> 00:10:14.040
Pietro made an entry in his log though, describing
the strange entity and described it like “a

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:17.800
person stretched out… like the space around
them was stretched out, and they were being

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:19.709
stretched along with it…

00:10:19.709 --> 00:10:24.540
Their body went from the ground up to the
clouds, and their jaw swung at right angles.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:30.279
There were these gaps, as well, black gaps
in space around its body, like wings.”

00:10:30.279 --> 00:10:34.630
Foundation staff were fighting it, shooting
at this strange entity but their weapons had

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:36.139
no effect.

00:10:36.139 --> 00:10:42.680
This creature, this IT, is a being that inhabits
the human psychosphere - meaning it exists

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:47.959
within the minds of all humans on some level,
driving and manipulating them to mysterious

00:10:47.959 --> 00:10:49.019
ends.

00:10:49.019 --> 00:10:50.160
What can it do?

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.350
What does it want?

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:56.149
It seems that the only people who know are
the O5 Council and the Foundation Ethics Committee

00:10:56.149 --> 00:10:58.790
who were privy to the PNEUMA report.

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:03.420
But whatever it was they saw, they believed
it was worth killing off all of humanity just

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:04.750
to stop it.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:09.199
As indicated by the unanimous vote from the
Ethics Committee, omnicide was a more ethical

00:11:09.199 --> 00:11:11.920
choice compared to the alternative.

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:16.750
The influence of IT was also likely what gave
Pietro the strong, subconscious desire to

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:25.529
unite the briefcase containing SCP - 055 with
SCP - 579 - even at the cost of his own life.

00:11:25.529 --> 00:11:28.300
This brings us to our final questions:

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:35.600
Why was it so important to unite SCP - 055
and SCP- 579, and what did this act serve

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:36.879
to achieve?

00:11:36.879 --> 00:11:41.869
As Pietro, wounded by the Blinkers and lingering
on the edge of death, finally delivered the

00:11:41.869 --> 00:11:47.569
briefcase into 579’s containment chamber,
he acknowledged the fact that he was no hero.

00:11:47.569 --> 00:11:50.339
But that’s where Pietro was wrong.

00:11:50.339 --> 00:11:55.049
After the destruction of SCP - 2000, Pietro
was in control of one of the only remaining

00:11:55.049 --> 00:11:57.549
ways to save the world.

00:11:57.549 --> 00:12:03.049
The combination of the anomalous effects of
055 and 579, as laid out in Roget’s Proposal

00:12:03.049 --> 00:12:09.300
and the article for SCP - 2998, is the Foundation’s
ultimate trump card for preventing an XK-Class

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:11.709
end of the world scenario.

00:12:11.709 --> 00:12:17.100
If the two are united during said scenario,
the universe resets to a time before the XK

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:20.320
Class scenario began, and prevents it from
happening.

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:25.129
In this case, Pietro uniting the two created
a new reality where the PNEUMA Project was

00:12:25.129 --> 00:12:31.220
never launched, and IT was never discovered
- thereby averting the apocalypse.

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:37.339
The corpse of poor dead Pietro and the highly
damaged SCP - 5000 suit he wore were the only

00:12:37.339 --> 00:12:41.230
evidence that this alternate reality ever
existed.

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:45.839
This means that the collaboration between
Pietro Wilson and the suit he just happened

00:12:45.839 --> 00:12:50.649
to stumble upon quite literally saved the
universe as we know it from a Foundation that

00:12:50.649 --> 00:12:52.429
had gone rogue.

00:12:52.429 --> 00:12:57.209
In this regard, he’s one of the greatest
heroes the universe has ever known, even if

00:12:57.209 --> 00:13:00.290
his actions weren’t entirely his own.

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:05.939
After all, he got a helping hand from the
suit, and another from IT - who still lurks

00:13:05.939 --> 00:13:10.809
in all our minds, mercifully undiscovered,
to this day.

00:13:10.809 --> 00:13:15.019
What was IT’s grand plan or purpose that
triggered all the madness?

00:13:15.019 --> 00:13:20.149
Anyone who ever knew for sure resides in a
universe that no longer exists, and we can

00:13:20.149 --> 00:13:26.819
only hope that a history that never happened
is somehow unable to repeat itself in ours.

00:13:26.819 --> 00:13:32.910
And remember, check out our previous videos
on SCP - 5000 - The Suit to enjoy the epic

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:37.369
saga of Pietro Wilson’s journey through
a nightmare world with fresh eyes.

